{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato","suddhaso"],"title":"16. The Beloved","html":"<section class='range'  id='dhp209-220'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Khuddakanikāya </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Minor Collection </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Collection of Minor Texts </span></li>\n<li class='subdivision'><span class='root'>Dhammapada </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sayings of the Dhamma 209–220 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Verses of Dhamma </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='range-title'><span class='root'>Piyavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>16. The Beloved </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>The Preference Chapter </span></h1></header>\n<article id='dhp209'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Tayojanapabbajitavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ayoge yuñjamattānaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Applying yourself where you ought not, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>One who is dedicated to that which is not worthy of dedication, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>yogasmiñca ayojayaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>neglecting what you should be doing, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and who is not dedicated to that which is worthy of dedication, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Atthaṁ hitvā piyaggāhī, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>forgetting your goal, you cling to what you hold dear, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>has dropped the goal and grabbed their preferences - </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>pihetattānuyoginaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>jealous of those devoted to their heart’s goal. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>yet envies those who are intent upon self-development. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp210'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Mā piyehi samāgañchi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Don’t ever get too close </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Don’t get caught up in what you prefer </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>appiyehi kudācanaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>to those you like or dislike. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>or in what you do not prefer. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Piyānaṁ adassanaṁ dukkhaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>For not seeing the liked is suffering, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Not seeing what you prefer is hard to bear </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>appiyānañca dassanaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and so is seeing the disliked. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and so is seeing what you do not prefer. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp211'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tasmā piyaṁ na kayirātha, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Therefore don’t hold anything dear, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Therefore don’t form any preference; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>piyāpāyo hi pāpako; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>for it’s bad to lose those you love. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>loss of what one prefers is painful. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ganthā tesaṁ na vijjanti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>No ties are found in they who </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>One who has no attachments </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>yesaṁ natthi piyāppiyaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>hold nothing loved or loathed. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>has no preferences. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp212'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Aññatarakuṭumbikavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Piyato jāyatī soko, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sorrow springs from what we hold dear, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Sorrow is born from preference, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>piyato jāyatī bhayaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>fear springs from what we hold dear; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>fear is born from preference; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Piyato vippamuttassa, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>one free from holding anything dear </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>one who is free from preference </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>natthi soko kuto bhayaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>has no sorrow, let alone fear. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>has no sorrow and no fear. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp213'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Visākhāvatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Pemato jāyatī soko, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sorrow springs from attachment, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Sorrow is born from affection, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>pemato jāyatī bhayaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>fear springs from attachment; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>fear is born from affection; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Pemato vippamuttassa, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>one free from attachment </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>one who is free from affection </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>natthi soko kuto bhayaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>has no sorrow, let alone fear. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>has no sorrow and no fear. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp214'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Licchavīvatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ratiyā jāyatī soko, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sorrow springs from relishing, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Sorrow is born from partiality, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>ratiyā jāyatī bhayaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>fear springs from relishing; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>fear is born from partiality; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ratiyā vippamuttassa, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>one free from relishing </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>one who is free from partiality </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>natthi soko kuto bhayaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>has no sorrow, let alone fear. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>has no sorrow and no fear. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp215'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Anitthigandhakumāravatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Kāmato jāyatī soko, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sorrow springs from desire, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Sorrow is born from sensuality, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>kāmato jāyatī bhayaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>fear springs from desire; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>fear is born from sensuality; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Kāmato vippamuttassa, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>one free from desire </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>one who is free from sensuality </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>natthi soko kuto bhayaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>has no sorrow, let alone fear. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>has no sorrow and no fear. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp216'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Aññatarabrāhmaṇavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Taṇhāya jāyatī soko, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sorrow springs from craving, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Sorrow is born from craving, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>taṇhāya jāyatī bhayaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>fear springs from craving; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>fear is born from craving; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Taṇhāya vippamuttassa, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>one free from craving </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>one who is free from craving </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>natthi soko kuto bhayaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>has no sorrow, let alone fear. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>has no sorrow and no fear. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp217'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Pañcasatadārakavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sīladassanasampannaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>One accomplished in virtue and vision, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>One who has perfect morality and wisdom, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>dhammaṭṭhaṁ saccavedinaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>firmly principled, and truthful, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>who is established in the Dhamma and understands truth, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Attano kamma kubbānaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>doing oneself what ought be done: </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and who works on themself - </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>taṁ jano kurute piyaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>that’s who the people love. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>this is the kind of person that the populace prefers. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp218'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Ekaanāgāmittheravatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Chandajāto anakkhāte, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>One eager to realize the ineffable </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Interested in the inexpressible, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Manasā ca phuṭo siyā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>would be filled with awareness. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>with an expanded mind, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Kāmesu ca appaṭibaddhacitto, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Their mind not bound to pleasures of sense, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and not bound by sensuality - </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Uddhaṁsototi vuccati. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>they’re said to be heading upstream. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>such a one is said be going upstream. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp219'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Nandiyavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Cirappavāsiṁ purisaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>When a man returns safely </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>When a person who has been away for a long time </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>dūrato sotthimāgataṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>after a long time spent abroad, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>arrives safely from afar, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ñātimittā suhajjā ca, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>family, friends, and loved ones </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>their relatives, friends, and loved ones </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>abhinandanti āgataṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>celebrate his return. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>delight in that arrival. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp220'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tatheva katapuññampi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Just so, when one who has done good </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>In the same way, when one who has made merit </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>asmā lokā paraṁ gataṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>goes from this world to the next, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>goes from this world to the next, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Puññāni paṭigaṇhanti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>their good deeds receive them there, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>they are received by their merit </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>piyaṁ ñātīva āgataṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>as family welcomes home one they love. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>like the arrival of a beloved relative. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endvagga'><span class='root'>Piyavaggo soḷasamo. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></p></article></section>"}
